# Modelfile: Qwen3.5-9B (dense), 32K context — "32k-agentic" tuning, the
# default opencode-only tier for this model.
#
# opencode-only (Copilot CLI support dropped for qwen3.5:9b): Copilot CLI's
# static system+tool overhead measures ~21,504 input tokens (see
# docs/tuning-results.md) — 65% of this 32K window alone, which is why the
# qwen3.6:35b-a3b tiers needed to jump straight to 64K for Copilot CLI.
# opencode's default toolset (no bundled MCP) measures only ~7,322 input
# tokens — comfortably fits well inside 32K with plenty of headroom left
# for conversation/tool-context growth, so there's no need to pay this
# dense model's steep off-GPU speed penalty (see below) just to satisfy a
# client we're no longer using it with.
#
# Why 32768 and not 48K/64K: measured on this host (8GB VRAM, `ollama ps`,
# no num_gpu override) — qwen3.5:9b is DENSE (not MoE like
# qwen3.6:35b-a3b), so unlike that model it degrades hard once CPU
# offload starts (all 9.7B params run on whatever fraction lands on CPU,
# vs. MoE's ~3B active-only cost):
#
#   num_ctx    GPU split      gen tok/s   prompt-eval tok/s   size
#   32,768     81%/19% GPU    29.5        143.3               6.7 GB
#   49,152     78%/22% GPU    26.0        188.4               7.1 GB
#   65,536     74%/26% GPU    22.3         98.9               7.6 GB
#
# 32K keeps the best speed of the three "agentic" sizes while still
# leaving ~4-5x opencode's static overhead in headroom. See
# modelfiles/qwen3.5__9b-48k-agentic/Modelfile for the larger-context
# option (real /model mid-session switching in opencode, no restart
# needed) if a task needs more room. See docs/tuning-results.md
# ("qwen3.5:9b tuning") for the full writeup and the dense-vs-MoE finding
# behind this guidance.
#
# num_batch left at 256 — tested 128 (the fix that helps qwen3.6:35b-a3b
# at ≥96K) at 48K/64K for this model too; no measurable difference either
# time, so no reason to trade away prompt-eval throughput for it.
#
# num_gpu intentionally omitted — let Ollama's own auto-balancer pick
# layer placement from live free VRAM.

FROM qwen3.5:9b

PARAMETER num_ctx 32768
PARAMETER num_batch 256
PARAMETER num_thread 16

# Sampling aligned the same way as qwen3.5__9b-12k-standalone/Modelfile —
# see that file and docs/tuning-results.md ("Unsloth alignment") for the
# full reasoning.
PARAMETER temperature 0.6
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER presence_penalty 0.0

# 25% of num_ctx for output, matching the qwen3.6 agentic tiers'
# proportion (16384/65536, 32768/131072) — generous single-turn budget
# while leaving most of the window for accumulated conversation/tool
# context.
PARAMETER num_predict 8192

SYSTEM """You are a helpful assistant. Keep your internal reasoning
efficient and proportional to the difficulty of the question — do not
over-deliberate on simple requests. Regardless of how much you have
reasoned, always make sure to produce a clear, complete final answer
before you finish; if you notice you are running low on room to respond,
wrap up your reasoning early and give your best answer rather than leaving
it incomplete.
"""
